Z||000044||Ken Wittlief||06-15-2001||09:43 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroHeather:<BR><B>Uhhh...guys?  Are you saying when a couple gets married, they have LESS sex?  Is THAT what I have to look forward to?<P>What about all of those virgins who wait until they get married?  Does that mean once they DO get married, they have no sex still?!<P>Im getting married in the next couple of years, and Im TOTALLY looking forward to a healthy sexual relationship with my husband (I'm VERY monogamus).  Are you SURE that sex will die down (once I start getting some)?  Any other things that I should prepare for in marriage??</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Studies have show that couples that wait to have sex until after they are married have the best and most rewarding sex lives.<P>  has to do with how the woman feels about herself, and the level of commitment and priorities. <P>  so in a very real way, couples that have sex before they are married (for what, a year of so?) mess up their sex lives for the other 20, 30, 40 years.<P>  I guess its kinda like you build a car engine and you cant wait to drive it, so you try it out first before you put the oil in, and then put the oil in later, when you get around to it.<P>  Usually it has no effect on the husbands attitude towards sex - its the wife that feels cheap and used.<P>  the real kiss of death for a marriage is the "Your what?! then I guess we better get married!" marrage proposal. Every single couple I have ever met that was expecting when they got married is now divorced (I can think of 8 off the top of my head). that includes 'honeymoon babies' - ( ie. your 2nd, 3rd, 4th... children all take 9 months, but the first one can come at any time :-O<P>  another statistic that seems odd at first, but makes sense when you think about it, another group of women that have excellent sex lives are fundementalist Bible believeing Christians. It appears they have taken great effort and expend a lot of attention on the importance of the marriage relationship, and the sexual relationship with their husband is one of the things they feel fully free to enjoy and explore, like its part of the reward a couple gets for being a great couple.<P>   go figure.||||reg||1
