Z||000058||Ken Wittlief||06-18-2001||11:03 AM||||the real reason for it is:<P>  sex can lead to children (in spite of modern birth control)<P>  children need a mother and father<P>  women take the role of parent much more seriously - esp when they are pregnant (in general - not case by case)<P>  therefore:<P>   if a women is already married to a man she loves and wants to spend her life with, a child is a blessing - so she doesnt have to be afraid to get pregnant - it may not be what she wants right now (may have career plans...) but if it happens its not the end of the world.<P>   a woman who is not married, if she gets pregnant, then what? Marry someone you werent ready to marry yet? (if you were ready you would be). Abortion? Single mother?<P>  this may sound silly but as humans we NEED to have ONLY one reason to do something. If we marry someone we NEED it to be because we love them and want to spend the rest of our lives with them.<P>  Not because they were the first person we had sex with, and now we feel obligated.<P>  and esp not because a child is now on the way. <P>  we experence this in all kinds of stuff. You can have a job you really love, or you can have the job that brings in the most money, but if you take a job for the money you will almost always end up hating your job.<P>  but personally I think the most important thing that affects the way a wife feels about herself, is if her BF, fiance, mate, makes it clear by his actions and conduct, that he is willing to wait and put off sex until after marriage so there is no doubt in her mind that she is the most important thing in the world to him, not sex, not beauty, not money, not anything else.<P>  then no matter what happens (for better or worse - sometimes worse really happens) he will always be there, by her side.||||reg||1
