Z||000072||FieroHeather||06-21-2001||03:37 PM||||Having a purely physical relationship is very unrealistic in the real world, even though the "real world" wants you to think that that's what you are supposed to be having!  Its those fricken advertisers I tell ya!  They use sex to sell things, but they either forget or dont care that inducing that kind of mentality in people is actually harmful to most relationships.<P>I am TOTALLY looking forward to being married and having sex at least once a day for the first 30 or so years.  But until then, I am working with my fiancee on building up other areas of our relationship--the stuff that matters in the real world.  I think I would be classified under Ken's catergory of a person enjoying the reward to explore the sexual side of the relationship freely (in the marriage context) and without the "guilt" factor.  Guilt sucks.  I want freedom! I also want sex! And lots of it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
