Z||000078||poupas||06-21-2001||05:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>engagement is a agreement or intention to make a commitment - you are still free to back out if you chose.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>  When you are engaged you should be just as commited as when you are married. You are still free to back out when you are married, the difference being you have to do it legally. Also if you have been living with the person for long enough you are considered common-law, and would still have to go through the legal proceedings as if you were married.<BR>  If you got to the point of engagement, you should know, with no doubt in your mind, that this person is the one for you. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000079||Nashco||06-21-2001||06:33 PM||||poupas...SHOULD is the operative word there.  Of course, lots of things SHOULD be a certain way, but how society is just doesn't tend to follow that rational.  There are a lot of screwy people out there; I agree, if I get engaged with somebody I know that I'm absolutely serious about it, but I won't know that they're 100% until we actually get married.  That's the whole point of being engaged...show that you are serious and have *intent* to get married.  If you decide it's not going to work, then you can still back out (of course you'll still feel sh1tty about it, but that's better than living with it for the rest of your life).  Also, once you're married you SHOULDn't get a divorce, according to the vows you make when you get married, but hey, that's another part of life.  This is just my take on this poupas, nothing personal or anything like that.<P>Little off subject, but somebody answer me this:  Why is every single thing you do held accountable (what you say, write, build, use, see, etc) in a lawsuit, but if you say you're going to commit yourself to your husband/wife for the rest of your life, that somehow doesn't count as much????  I mean, I know there are pre-nup agreements, but doesn't it seem odd that you can bail even though you promised you would do something?  How would the credit card company react if I told them I thought I would have loved to pay my bill every month, but after a couple years I decided it wasn't for me?  Silly humans....what the hell is wrong with us? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Oh, one more quick thing... <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>I want freedom! I also want sex! And lots of it!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE> My ears perked up like a puppy's when you said that <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Amen!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||5
Z||000080||FieroHeather||06-21-2001||11:49 PM||||I agree with Ken and Nashco that Engagement is the time period to show a serious commitment to the person you intend to marry--and it should be treated at the same level of committment as the level of committment in a marriage as per poupas' comment.<P>But backing out of a marriage is NOT an option for me.  When I marry, it is for better or worse.  I pray that it is for the better, but I know that there will be hard times ahead--life is just like that.  I am not a quitter, and my friends can agree with me on that one.  I guess it is part of my stubbornness.  If I wasnt stubborn, I wouldnt have been together with the love of my life right now.  Some say it is perseverence, I call it stubbornness!<P>I also do not want to give my body away to many different guys through the sexual act, but I save my body for my husband--it is HIS present  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  What more do I have to give to him other than myself?||||reg||1
Z||000081||Nashco||06-22-2001||12:10 AM||||Just to clarify myself, incase I came across different that what I meant to..<P>I am completely against divorce; that was why I didn't understand why it is even acceptable.  That is my personal feeling about marriage, because I think there is a point of seriousness that you shouldn't be able to back out of.  If I think it's serious enough to get married, I damn sure better think about it and realize the immensity of the decision.<P>My parents have been married since two years before I was born (I'm the oldest of four kids over a ten year spread).  They went through some *very* hard times, but have worked everything out and have very good lives and a very healthy relationship now.  Especially with the mechanical/engineering mind I'm constantly developing, I think anything can be fixed...even relationships.<P>I think marriage is the second most serious issue people have to deal with today, having children being the most important.  I get soooo pissed when I see people treat these issues as if they were trying to pick the paint color for their house.  I especially hate to see people who have five or six marriages, or way too many kids; I don't understand how people can think that way.  Another facet of life I guess we all see.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000082||87 Pegasus||06-22-2001||12:48 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by poupas:<BR><B>   <BR>  About the Fierosex fetish, just imagine you and your mate getting the urges while you are driving, stop and park for awhile. Have sex somewhere other than the bedroom. It breaks up routine and is alot of fun.<BR>   <BR>  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>yeah like he said it breaks routine... it is like the people who have sex in elevators, stockrooms, etc... i think every once in awhile you have to do something out of routine to spice your sex life up again...  why do the same thing over and over again...soon it gets old and out dated...  i am not saying go have sex in the mall elevator but try something out of routine...  for the people who say they do not get enough because it is the same thing over and over try something new...  it never hurts to try in first...  and for the poeple who like to wait til they are married good for you... but that could always back fire... because later you may wonder could it be better?  is it different with another?  is there different ways?  you just have to wonder...so just be careful it could  just pop in there...  like Ray in Ghostbusters with the State Puff Marshmellon Man... It Just Popped in there...  you never know just a for warning...  play it safe...  it is your call.... <P><P>------------------<BR>Friends don't let friends drive Corvettes!!||||reg||3
