Z||000115||BAM-BAM||06-25-2001||10:09 PM|||| Don't usually entertain this section of the Forum. But this post, for obvious reasons peaked my interest. So to further expound on the theories of sex in Fiero's and sex after marriage and the apparent need for some to wait untill marriage, just let me add. <P>Sex in a Fiero? Yes it is entirely possible and rather enjoyable.<P>Sex after marriage? sorry to burst anyones bubble, but it's a gonner. One of the parties will soon lose interst after the comfort guarentee has been inacted. <BR>Rationale- While dating and engaged, there is still the uncertainty of commitment. With that uncertainty, we try harder to ensure that we won't lose the one we want. for what ever reason/s we want them. After the rings are in place and the liscense is on the wall, it's time to relax. Now we don't have to work as hard at keeping something that we now deem as ours. Sorry, but it's usually the woman.<P>Waiting untill marriage? Do what you want, but when you look back and realize that things aren't as you planned (how ever hard you planned it) Just remember it was your choice. <P>I have been married three times to three women that I truly loved. Every time it has come down to the same thing. "That's all you want". Well, no, that's not all I want, I just want what we had before the rings went on. I'm on my third marriage now and it's no different. If I had it to do all over, I would date untill it got stupid (talk of marriage) and bolt. There is a certain majic in the dating proccess that you won't find in marriage. I wish it weren't true but those are the majority facts. As someone in an earlier post mentioned, it's all because of the Media and advertisement pushing the bigger better deal. Now no one will ever be satisfied with what they have. You'll always here about something better. Just my 2 cents.<P>Sorrry, b2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>||||reg||9
