Z||000117||Steve Normington||06-26-2001||11:14 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B> I am gonna stay away from that one - even I wouldn't cross THAT LINE!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Coward!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000118||Ken Wittlief||06-26-2001||11:26 AM||||BamBam,<P> lets see if I got this straight. You've been married three times. had sex with each wife before you got married. all three wives apparently think your primary interest is sex (whether it acutally is or not - thats how THEY feel).<P>  and after each marriage the sex life went down the tubes.<P> Hmmmmmmmmmm...<P>EDIT: i looked at this again and I am tempted to delete it - I realize this is a little personal for you. Im not trying to get on your case or make lite of your situation.<P>  I work as an engineer - an interesting job in that when I try to do something and it doesnt work out like I thought it should, then its silly for me to curse the laws of physic or wonder if they have changed since yesterday.<P>  so in my work, if something goes wrong its always the engineers fault - always something I did wrong - ego goes out the window the first time an engineer makes a mistake. I think I carry this over into my personal life to.<P>   If you are on marriage #3 then maybe its time to take a look back and see what went wrong. I think one of the problems we have with raising kids is we dont tell them the mistakes we made, the lessons we learned the hard way - we simply say, "Dont do that!" why? because - just dont!<P>  My wife and I lived together for a year before we got married, for a lot of 'good reasons'. Now, 21 years later, we can both look back and realize that was a major mistake. For us to go through this 21 year process, and not share with others what we have learned the hard way, would be selfish.<P>  I think if more people would stand up and tell young people, I know what you are feeling, I know how it looks to you from where you are now - but there are aspects to this that you wont understand till later, or until you mess things up and you cant go back - And I know because I did it the wrong way and suffered the consequences.<P>  So I hope you dont mind too much if I take what you posted as a perfect example of the same mistakes I made. This tradition going back thousands of years of waiting to have sex until after you are married has alot more to it than pregnacy - birth control has not made it a non-issue.<P>   And personally, for myself and my wife, it made a big difference in our marriage when I realized that us living together before we got married was a mistake - when we talked about it - and when I made extensive efforts to show my wife that sex is not the primary reason I married her.<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 06-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000119||Steve Normington||06-26-2001||02:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>This tradition going back thousands of years of waiting to have sex until after you are married has alot more to it than pregnacy - birth control has not made it a non-issue.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, in days of yore, the point of having sex being okay was the engagement. That was the original purpose of the diamond ring - payment for the female's virginity if the couple did not get married.<P>Just a chance for me to show off my store of useless knowledge, I agree with your point.||||reg||1
