Z||000142||Her86GT||06-30-2001||09:07 PM||||I think people who wait until they're married to have sex have the right idea.  Besides, it is intended to be shared with the person you spend the rest of your life with.  But - this rarely happens.  My theory is that people who wait to have sex until they are married just put a big strain on the relationship.  This could cause the couple to "get married for the wrong reasons" so-to-speak.  I've only ever had sex with my husband and vice versa.  We are each others first and we didn't wait until marriage - unfortunalty.  But there are no trust issues because we don't know what it would be like to be with other people.  Kinda like still being a virgin.  So, waiting or not until marriage is a decision a couple should make, not an individual decision.  If you meet someone and date for a while and feel like marriage could be possible, sex is like completing the emotional connection - not something that should be expected after the first kiss. . .||||reg||1
